//- The Search and Multi-Selection controls of a second top header bar.
//-
//- ONE copy of each, used by both bars that have them: the board header of the
//- Swimlanes view (boardHeader.jade) and the All Boards header bar
//- (boardsList.jade). They had drifted - All Boards carried a search FIELD
//- while a board carried a search BUTTON, and the two Multi-Selection buttons
//- were the same markup written out twice, already differing in the tooltip of
//- their ✕.
//-
//- Only the MARKUP is shared. What a click does is not: on a board, Search
//- searches cards and Multi-Selection selects cards; on All Boards both work on
//- boards, and the two pages keep their own selection object and their own
//- sidebar. That works because a Blaze event map catches events from the
//- templates rendered inside it, so `Template.boardHeaderBar.events` and
//- `Template.boardListHeaderBar.events` each see the clicks on their own copy.
//-
//- docs/Design/Page/Search.md, docs/Design/Page/Multi-Selection.md

template(name="headerSearchButton")
  a.board-header-btn.js-open-search-view(title="{{_ 'search'}}")
    i.fa.fa-search
    span {{_ 'search'}}

//- `isActive` is passed in, because the two pages select different things and
//- so keep different selection objects: MultiSelection (cards) on a board,
//- BoardMultiSelection (boards) on All Boards.
template(name="headerMultiSelectionButton")
  a.board-header-btn.js-multiselection-activate(
      title="{{#if isActive}}{{_ 'multi-selection-on'}}{{else}}{{_ 'multi-selection'}}{{/if}}"
      class="{{#if isActive}}emphasis{{/if}}")
    i.fa.fa-check-square-o
    span {{#if isActive}}{{_ 'multi-selection-on'}}{{else}}{{_ 'multi-selection'}}{{/if}}
    if isActive
      //- Turns Multi-Selection OFF. It said "Clear filter" on the board header,
        which is a different action entirely.
      a.board-header-btn-close.js-multiselection-reset(title="{{_ 'multi-selection-off'}}")
        i.fa.fa-times-thin
